1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,380
Reading Tosk

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:05,000
Iqbaluit

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,800
The Frozen Town

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,460
The reporter Beth Allen arrived in a northern community called Iqbaluit in Nunavut.

5
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:22,620
Nunavut was created in 1999 as a special area for Inuit people.

6
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:26,820
Its name means "Our Land" in their language.

7
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:31,300
It is in the farthest northeastern area of Canada,

8
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:33,340
north of the Arctic Circle(北极圈),

9
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:40,700
and is very cold - the average winter temperature in Nunavut is 35 degrees below zero.

10
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:45,720
Beth said, "I knew it would be cold in January,

11
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,320
but not this cold!

12
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:53,580
Maybe there is a dog sled (雪橇) that can take me into town." The quiet man who

13
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:54,640
had been on the plane

14
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:57,480
with her said, "I’ll take you into town,

15
00:00:57,860 --> 00:00:59,860
but I don’t have a dog sled.

16
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:04,200
Most people only use the dogs for competitions.

17
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:25,120
My name is Simon and I am Inuit," he said.

18
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:30,960
I think it’s too far north here for holidays but more and more tourists are coming.

19
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:34,880
They like ice fishing and photographing polar bears.

20
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:38,960
I stay as far away from polar bears as possible.

21
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:44,240
I like my warm office and my warm house." Beth asked, "

22
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,780
What do you do in an office?

23
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:49,700
Don’t you hunt animals for a living?

24
00:01:55,780 --> 00:02:00,100
My grandfather would live in ice houses when he hunted in winter,

25
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,700
but not so many people do that now.

26
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:06,240
The old men used to make one in a few hours.

27
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:33,900
Beth said, "Why is it so dark?

28
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:37,940
It’s the middle of the day!" Simon replied, "

29
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:41,820
It’s dark in the day because we are so far north.

30
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,900
You should come in June.

31
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:47,780
The sun shines all night in the north then.

32
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:51,800
That’s why it’s called ’The Land of the Midnight Sun’."

33
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:54,220
There were people on the streets

34
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:56,080
and snowmobiles everywhere.

35
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,920
There were even a few dog teams.
